From 2b24bc2287e5e05bad628d1cb1d17f9a73670f4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:25:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/38] hydra: read Houdini op: texture paths by cooking the
 COP during sync

A texture path can name a compositing node rather than a file. Nothing hands
those pixels over as a file - the USD asset resolver returns an asset of size
zero, and Houdini's own image layer refuses the path outright, both measured -
so the node has to be cooked. Do that while the prim is being synced and give
Cycles the resulting image, leaving the normal loader untouched for ordinary
paths.

Cooking deliberately happens at sync time rather than in the image loader:
loading runs on Cycles' worker threads, and cooking a Houdini node from one of
those would take the host down. Results are cached per path, and the call is
guarded so a batch render - which has no hou module at all - reports a plain
warning naming the path instead of raising.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
